# .gitignore — shared DevSecOps cluster-ops workspace
# Policy: almost everything is shared as-is (knowledge, playbooks, scans, templates, hooks, audit
# trail). Only what must NOT sync is excluded.

# 1) Regenerable dependencies — never sync (rebuild with: npm --prefix templates/reports install)
node_modules/

# 2) Transient runtime state — must NOT propagate to teammates.
#    state/APPROVE_NEXT is a SINGLE-USE destructive-command approval token; syncing it could
#    auto-approve a destructive kubectl on someone else's machine.
state/

# 3) FULL command logs — LOCAL ONLY. They capture full command OUTPUT, which can contain secrets
#    (get secret -o yaml, env dumps, tokens). The SHAREABLE record is audit/ (metadata only), which
#    IS committed.
logs/

# 4) Rendered report deliverables are regenerable from the .md source; keep the repo lean.
#    (Comment this out if you prefer to commit the .docx deliverables.)
reports/*.docx

# 5) Anything a team marks local-only (credentials staged for a human, device-specific notes):
#    name them *.local.* and they never sync.
*.local.txt
*.local.md
*.local.json
.*-token
